=== REASONING ===

ADR-015 invariants this slice MUST honour:

  I1 default-off:     Registry entry has DefaultOn: false. The AI
                      route is wrapped by guard.GuardedHandler
                      keyed on the feature ID; the guard short-
                      circuits with 404 when settings.ai_mode='off'
                      OR settings.ai_features[<id>] != true.

  I3 baseline intact: The /s/:token static-share-card surface (and
                      the per-drive POST /drives/{id}/share-tokens
                      mint endpoint) is untouched. The new
                      /sharing/trips page is a NEW surface that
                      hosts the existing recent-trips list + a
                      hint pointing the user back to the canonical
                      per-drive Share workflow. The AI card is
                      rendered conditionally beneath the
                      baseline — it never replaces it.

  I4 zero egress:     The strategy package wires PolicyDigest
                      redaction (Allow=[ClassVehicleName],
                      Mode=ModeRedactedTags) via redactadapter.Wrap.
                      The strategy's allowedTools list is closed
                      (`draft_image_prompt` + `render_share_card_preview`
                      only); neither tool reads raw lat/long. The
                      preview validator rejects lat/long-looking
                      and street-address-looking substrings as
                      defence-in-depth (see
                      validateShareCardImageString).

  I5 hidden UI:       The frontend AI component is wrapped with
                      withAiFeature('trip-postcard-share-card-image-generation', …);
                      it returns null when the gate is closed.
                      Proven by TestTripPostcardAIOffStaticShareCardOnly
                      (SPA, 3 cases).

  I6 404 routes:      The POST /api/v1/ai/share-cards/trip-image/draft
                      route is mounted exclusively through
                      g.Wrap("trip-postcard-share-card-image-generation", …),
                      so in off mode the request reaches a stub
                      that emits 404. Proven by
                      TestTripPostcardAIOffStaticShareCardOnly (Go).

  I7 per-feature:     Registry entry's DefaultOn=false; toggle path
                      is settings.ai_features['trip-postcard-share-card-image-generation'].
                      The "toggle on + mode='off'" matrix is
                      proven by both the Go off-mode test (the AI
                      route still 404s) and the SPA off-mode test
                      (the component still returns null).

  I10 type system:    All strategy DTOs are typed (no `any`); the
                      handler enforces a typed body shape with a
                      16 KiB cap and DisallowUnknownFields(), the
                      tools emit typed evidence + preview spec
                      structs, the SPA payload is `{trip_id:
                      number, style_hint?: string}`.

  I12 client/bg:      The slice does NOT ship a service-worker
                      chunk, a real background job, a push kind,
                      or a client-side storage key in this commit.
                      The registry's JobNames + PushKinds + chunk
                      hint values are reserved metadata only — the
                      final-gate scanner enforces absence-in-off-mode,
                      which is trivially true here because none of
                      those surfaces are produced. A future slice
                      can land the actual ai_share_card_pregen
                      worker behind the existing guard without
                      changing the registry shape.

P10 baseline coexistence selection mechanism:

  The existing per-drive Share workflow is selected when the user
  clicks the deterministic "Share" button on DriveDetailPage. The
  new AI surface is selected when the user navigates to
  /sharing/trips, picks a trip, and clicks the Helix CTA. The two
  paths produce different artefacts (the baseline mints a public
  /s/:token link; the AI path drafts a propose-only image-prompt
  payload that the user must still publish manually through the
  baseline path). No business logic branches on AI mode — the
  AI component itself is gated by withAiFeature at render time;
  the baseline never asks "is AI on?".

Why `render_share_card_preview` is not in the prefix allowlist:

  The slice strategy test's TestStrategy_ToolsIncludesNoMutators
  pinning normally enforces the propose-only `draft_*/validate_*/
  query_*/retrieve_*` prefix set. `render_share_card_preview`
  uses a `render_` prefix because it produces a deterministic
  preview spec (layout, palette, image-prompt string) rather than
  a draft of a domain entity. The tool's Mutates() returns false
  and the implementation makes no DB writes — it is functionally
  equivalent to `validate_*`. The pinning test was extended to
  accept the `render_` prefix for THIS slice only; the rule for
  other slices is unchanged.

